ow renders a single \"Failed\" state with status.message text as supplementary detail.\n- State visuals match the approved UX specification.\n\nHLR: P0-2; fallback for P2.\n\nBranch epics:\n\nBRANCH-A-E005: detail-polling data layer.\n\n# Detail-Polling Data Layer for Visible-Page Evaluation Jobs\n\nDescription: Implement the second polling layer in the eval-hub-ui plugin that fetches the detail endpoint (GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}) for in-progress jobs visible on the currently displayed table page, providing per-benchmark status data for progress display. Exists only if the investigation confirms status.benchmarks[] is populated mid-run.\n\nScope: new detail-polling hook following the React Query retry-with-backoff pattern established by the autorag package (placeholderData preserving last successful response, exponential backoff with jitter up to max retries, 4xx non-retryable, 5xx/network retried); 10-second cycle that starts after all detail fetches for the current page complete; round-robin dispatch capped at 5 concurrent requests; only jobs on the current visible table page (client-side pagination, default 20 rows, options 5/10/20) in non-terminal states are polled, updating immediately when the page changes; Page Visibility API pause when tab backgrounded with an immediate single cycle on resume; expose error state for the warning UI while continuing to show last successful data; verify the odh-dashboard BFF proxy transparently passes all detail response fields (no code change expected — validation only), including simulating 5xx responses from the BFF to validate retry behavior in the Module Federation context.\n\nAC:\n- Only jobs in non-terminal state on the currently displayed table page are polled via the detail endpoint; changing the page immediately retargets polling.\n- At most 5 detail requests are in flight concurrently; as one completes the next pending job is fetched (round-robin).\n- A 10-second timer starts only when all detail fetches for