{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-5922e55b-3f4e-47c7-96ae-6def7befef33","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9af34bb21205f78e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-yo4xeveb/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-decomposition.md","content":"# Decomposition Summary: RHAISTRAT-8005 — EvalHub UI: Real-Time Evaluation Job Progress and State Visibility\n\n## Triage Outcome\n\nThe strategy is S-sized, single active component (eval-hub-ui plugin), effectively single implementing team (ODH Dashboard). However, it contains two explicit open questions flagged \"needs validation\" in the strategy's Assumptions and Open Questions tables, and each answer changes which downstream epics exist or what they do (mid-run detail polling and benchmark-progress display hinge on whether `status.benchmarks[]` is populated mid-run; the P2 failure distinction hinges on `status.message.message_code` values). The genuine-unknowns escape condition applies — full decomposition with Investigation epics proceeds.\n\n## Staff Engineer Input Overrides (Step 1.5 traceability)\n\nThe Staff Engineer Input takes precedence over the AI-generated Technical Approach. The following directives were incorporated:\n\n1. **No new API data**: The plan assumes no data beyond what the existing list (`GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs`) and detail (`GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}`) endpoints currently provide. No server-side changes; out-of-scope items reinforced.\n2. **List vs. detail field inventory**: The Staff field table (description, tags, `status.benchmarks[]`, mlflow_run_id, logs_path, per-benchmark parameters/pass_criteria available only in the detail response) is authoritative for the progress model.\n3. **Visible-page-only polling**: Only jobs on the currently displayed table page (client-side pagination, default 20 rows, options 5/10/20 per `tablePaginationConstants.ts`) are detail-polled; page turns retarget polling immediately.\n4. **Concurrency**: Maximum 5 parallel detail fetches, round-robin (next job dispatched as one completes); the 10-second timer starts only when all calls for the current page complete.\n5. **Retry pattern**: Replicate the autorag/automl React Query retry-with-exponential-backoff pattern; non-blocking warning while last successful status remains displayed.\n6. **Resolved questions**: 10-second latency is sufficient; Page Visibility API pause confirmed; scalability deferred for this release (all user polling behavior identical).\n\nTwo unknowns remain open after the Staff review (both listed in the strategy's Open Questions table, owner TrustyAI / EvalHub team) and become Investigation epics.\n\n## Component Name Mappings (canonical names from `.context/rhai-components.txt`)\n\n| Strategy component | Canonical component | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| eval-hub-ui (odh-dashboard plugin) | AI Evaluations | Closest canonical name for the EvalHub UI work |\n| EvalHub Server API (data-availability questions) | AI Evaluations | Investigation subject |\n| odh-dashboard (BFF) | AI Evaluations (passive) | No code change expected; same owning team as the active component, so BFF field-passthrough validation is an acceptance criterion on the detail-polling epic, not a separate epic |\n| Dashboard design system (UX/Design) | UXD | UX specification epic |\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| RHAISTRAT-8005-E001 | Investigation: mid-run population of `status.benchmarks[]` in the detail endpoint | Investigation | TrustyAI / EvalHub | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8005-E002 | Investigation: `status.message.message_code` values for pre-start vs. runtime failures | Investigation | TrustyAI / EvalHub | P2 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8005-E003 | UX specification for evaluation job state and progress indicators | Implementation | UX/Design | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8005-E004 | Evaluation job state visual differentiation in the EvalHub UI | Implementation | ODH Dashboard | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8005-BRANCH-A-E005 | Detail-polling data layer for visible-page evaluation jobs (branch A) | Implementation | ODH Dashboard | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8005-BRANCH-A-E006 | Benchmark progress, elapsed time, and polling warning display (branch A) | Implementation | ODH Dashboard | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8005-BRANCH-A-E007 | Pre-start vs. runtime failure state distinction (branch A of the failure-code investigation) | Implementation | ODH Dashboard | P2 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8005-BRANCH-B-E005 | Elapsed time display from job creation timestamp (branch B) | Implementation | ODH Dashboard | P1 |\n\nMain plan: E001–E004. Branch epics (BRANCH-A-E005/E006/E007, BRANCH-B-E005) are conditional units attached to their gating Investigations, not standalone Jira issues.\n\n## Dependency DAG (main plan)\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[\"E001 Investigation: benchmarks[] mid-run population\"]\n    E002[\"E002 Investigation: message_code failure values\"]\n    E003[\"E03 UX specification for state and progress indicators\"]\n    E004[\"E04 Evaluation job state visual differentiation UI\"]\n    E003 --> E004\n```\n\n### Conditional branches\n\n**Branch A of E001** (outcome: `status.benchmarks[]` is populated while a job is running — detail polling has mid-run value):\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[\"E001 Investigation\"] --> AE005[\"BRANCH-A-E005 Detail-polling data layer\"]\n    AE005 --> AE006[\"BRANCH-A-E006 Progress and elapsed time display\"]\n    E002[\"E002 Investigation\"] --> AE007[\"BRANCH-A-E007 Pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction\"]\n```\n\n**Branch B of E001** (outcome: `status.benchmarks[]` populated only after completion — no mid-run detail polling; elapsed time from `resource.created_at`):\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[\"E001 Investigation\"] --> BE005[\"BRANCH-B-E005 Elapsed time display from created_at\"]\n```\n\n**Branch B of E002** (outcome: `message_code` does not reliably distinguish pre-start from runtime failures): no branch epic — the strategy's documented fallback (single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail) is an acceptance criterion on E004.\n\nNote on branch-epic edges: the branch-epic dependency convention restricts branch `dependencies` to the gating Investigation plus sibling branch epics, so two coordination dependencies that cannot be expressed as DAG edges are recorded here and in the epic bodies instead: (1) the branch-A display epic renders data exposed by the branch-A polling epic (expressed as the E005→E006 sibling edge), and (2) all display epics consume the UX specification produced by E003.\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| E003 → E004 | 12/13 (artifact → consumer) | The state UI builds against the UX specification's icon/color/label decisions; serializing avoids rework. |\n| E001 → BRANCH-A-E005, BRANCH-A-E006, BRANCH-B-E005 | 3 (Investigation gate, bounded outcome) | Whether `status.benchmarks[]` is populated mid-run decides whether the detail-polling layer and benchmark-progress display exist at all (branch A) or degrade to elapsed-time-only from list data (branch B). Two bounded outcomes → conditional branches. |\n| E002 → BRANCH-A-E007 | 3 (Investigation gate, bounded outcome) | Whether `message_code` values distinguish pre-start from runtime failures decides whether the P2 distinction feature exists; fallback (single \"Failed\" + message text) is an AC on E004. |\n| BRANCH-A-E005 → BRANCH-A-E006 | 12/13 (framework → consumer) | The display components consume the polling hook's data and error state; sibling edge within branch A. |\n| No edge E001/E002 ↔ E003/E004 | 14 (independent) | State differentiation from the list endpoint's `status.state` is independent of both data-availability unknowns and of the UX spec timeline. |\n| No edge between E001 and E002 | 14 | Independent unknowns, different questions and deliverables; combining them would create a 4-outcome branch matrix. |\n| No edge from BFF validation | Passive component rule | odh-dashboard BFF needs no code change; same owning team as the active component → acceptance criterion on the detail-polling epic. |\n| No `konflux-onboarding` / `repo-onboarding` epics | 20 | eval-hub-ui plugin already onboarded; work happens in the existing odh-dashboard repo. |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Auto-refresh mechanism (list polling for top-level state + detail polling for progress) | P0 | BRANCH-A-E005 (new detail-polling layer); top-level state auto-refresh is existing 30s list-endpoint polling, verified as an AC on E004. Under branch B, this HLR is met by the existing list polling (no new detail polling has mid-run value). |\n| Visual distinction of queued/running/failed/completed states | P0 | E004 |\n| Non-blocking error handling during detail polling | P0 | BRANCH-A-E005 (retry/backoff, last-success preservation), BRANCH-A-E006 (inline warning display) |\n| Benchmark-level progress display (X/N) | P1 | BRANCH-A-E006 (branch A only; not implementable mid-run under branch B — see branch gate) |\n| Elapsed time display | P1 | BRANCH-A-E006 (from per-benchmark `started_at`), BRANCH-B-E005 (from `resource.created_at` under branch B) |\n| Page Visibility pause/resume of polling | P1 | BRANCH-A-E005 (scoped to detail polling per the strategy's technical approach; moot under branch B where no mid-run detail polling exists) |\n| Pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction | P2 | BRANCH-A-E007 (outcome A of the failure-code investigation); fallback single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text is an AC on E004 (outcome B) |\n\nAll seven HLRs are covered in every outcome branch.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **P0 scope is contingent on E001**: the only new P0 work under branch B is state differentiation (E004); P0-1/P0-3/P1-3 all attach to the detail-polling layer that exists only in branch A. Under branch B the strategy delivers substantially less than its P0 list implies, using existing list-polling behavior. PM/Engineering validation of the proposed acceptance criteria (flagged \"requires PM/Engineering validation\" in the strategy) should confirm this is acceptable.\n- **Unresolved human process gates**: Architecture Review, License Validation, UXD Support, and Performance Team Support are all \"Pending human review\" in the strategy's prerequisites table. These are human gates on the implementation epics, not decomposition blockers.\n- **Performance review risk**: the Performance Team's polling-load assessment is pending while the strategy explicitly defers scalability for this release. If that review later rejects the 5-concurrent-request cap or visible-page-only scoping, branch-A scope is rewritten.\n- **Module Federation validation risk** (strategy risk table): the autorag React Query retry pattern is untested in the eval-hub-ui Module Federation context. This does not change which epics exist or what they do (the pattern is adopted regardless; failure = fix-and-retry), so it is a validation acceptance criterion on the detail-polling epic, not an Investigation.\n- **Priority note**: E002 and BRANCH-A-E007 are P2 per priority inheritance (they enable only the P2 failure distinction). E001 is P0 because it gates P0 detail-polling work.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable — all external and internal dependencies (PatternFly, React Query, EvalHub Server APIs, BFF proxy path, Module Federation infrastructure) have status \"Exists\". No dependency has uncertain timing requiring a Tier 1/Tier 2 split.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45597,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92f56919d3942a78","agent_id":"af27bab92b4583410","session_id":"4d1cfcd2-7a48-4a97-8f21-5ac7a29e76ba","uuid":"e388f6c6-1322-4a3e-90e1-be554d2170b1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:3