{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e05b1d30-04c0-42cd-b139-1fa126591868","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd672a6662f55f81","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-yo4xeveb/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-E003.md","content":"# UX Specification for Evaluation Job State and Progress Indicators\n\n## Description\n\nProduce the UX/design specification for evaluation job state visuals and progress indicators on the EvalHub Evaluations landing page, fulfilling the \"progress indicator UX specification\" design doc listed as to-be-created in the strategy. The specification covers state icon/color/label treatments, the benchmark progress and elapsed time display pattern, the non-blocking warning pattern for temporarily unavailable status updates, and the visual treatment distinguishing pre-start failures from runtime failures. It is PatternFly-aligned and is the artifact the job-table UI implementation builds against.\n\n## Scope\n\n- State icon, color, and label specifications for queued/pending, running, failed, and completed job states, derived from the list endpoint's `status.state` field, using PatternFly status components (Label, Icon).\n- Visual treatment specification for the potential \"Failed (not started)\" pre-start failure distinction, distinct from the runtime \"Failed\" state.\n- Progress indicator pattern for benchmark-level progress (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\") including the single-benchmark case, where elapsed time acts as the primary progress indicator.\n- Elapsed time display pattern (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\").\n- Non-blocking inline warning pattern (PatternFly Alert, warning variant) shown while status updates are temporarily unavailable, with last successful data still displayed.\n- Progress indicator pattern review and PatternFly alignment check with the ODH Dashboard implementation team.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The specification defines distinct icon, color, and label for each of queued/pending, running, failed, and completed states, visually distinguishable from one another per the PatternFly status pattern.\n- The specification defines the benchmark progress display, elapsed time display, and the warning banner pattern, including behavior when only top-level state is available (before the first detail fetch returns).\n- The specification is reviewed and approved by UX/Design and the ODH Dashboard team.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Enables the P0 requirement for visual distinction between queued/pending, running, failed, and completed states.\n- Informs the visual design of the P1 benchmark-level progress display, P1 elapsed time display, and P2 pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":54912,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92f56919d3942a78","agent_id":"af27bab92b4583410","session_id":"4d1cfcd2-7a48-4a97-8f21-5ac7a29e76ba","uuid":"45b53224-6724-4408-bf7c-b4c3894ac3b8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:33:25.050Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
