{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c563cc4b-2955-423c-b0ab-974f5567be9f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a48c84d9bb94078a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-yo4xeveb/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-E004.md","content":"# Evaluation Job State Visual Differentiation in the EvalHub UI\n\n## Description\n\nImplement distinct visual treatments for queued/pending, running, failed, and completed evaluation job states in the job table on the EvalHub Evaluations landing page, derived from the list endpoint's `status.state` and `status.message` fields, per the approved UX specification. This work uses only data already returned by the existing list endpoint and leaves the existing 30-second list polling unchanged.\n\n## Scope\n\n- State badge rendering in the evaluations job table with a distinct PatternFly icon, color, and label for each state: Queued/Pending (`status.state` = `pending`), Running (active execution), Failed (with `status.message` providing error context), and Completed.\n- Supplementary display of `status.message` text for failed jobs.\n- Fallback rendering as a single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail for jobs whose failure type cannot be distinguished (the documented fallback when the failure-code classification is unavailable or ambiguous).\n- Verification that state labels update automatically within the existing list-endpoint polling interval (30 seconds) without manual browser refresh, using the existing `useEvaluationJobs` list polling.\n- Visual treatments implemented per the approved UX specification for state icons, colors, and labels.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an evaluation job is queued/pending (not yet started), when a user views the Evaluations landing page, then the job row displays a distinct \"Queued\" label and visual treatment visually distinguishable from \"Running\" and \"Failed\" states, measured by distinct icon, color, and label text per the PatternFly status pattern and the approved UX specification.\n- Given an evaluation job transitions from running to complete, when the user is on the Evaluations landing page without manually refreshing the browser, then the status update is visible within the list endpoint's polling interval (30 seconds), measured by the job list row updating its state label automatically.\n- Given a failed job whose failure type cannot be distinguished, when a user views the landing page, then the job row renders a single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail.\n- All state visuals match the approved UX specification.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Covers the P0 requirement for visual distinction between queued/pending, running, failed, and completed states.\n- Carries the fallback acceptance criterion for the P2 pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction (single \"Failed\" state with message text) for the case where failure codes do not reliably distinguish failure types.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":55552,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92f56919d3942a78","agent_id":"af27bab92b4583410","session_id":"4d1cfcd2-7a48-4a97-8f21-5ac7a29e76ba","uuid":"a345c858-8ef5-4bdc-924f-b35506dbef33","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:33:36.570Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
