{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-8a6e192b-338a-494f-8abe-d67d800d46c8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b51857858fc37c00","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-yo4xeveb/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-BRANCH-A-E005.md","content":"# Detail-Polling Data Layer for Visible-Page Evaluation Jobs\n\n## Description\n\nImplement the second polling layer in the eval-hub-ui plugin: a detail-polling hook that fetches the detail endpoint (`GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}`) for in-progress jobs visible on the currently displayed table page, obtaining `status.benchmarks[]` per-benchmark progress data for display. This epic exists only in the decomposition branch where the investigation confirms that `status.benchmarks[]` is populated while a job is still running; under the alternative outcome, mid-run detail polling has no value and is not built.\n\n## Scope\n\n- New detail-polling hook in the eval-hub-ui plugin following the React Query retry-with-backoff pattern established by the autorag package (`usePipelineRunQuery`): `placeholderData` preserving the last successful response during transient errors, retry with exponential backoff (`RETRY_DELAY_MS * 2^attempt` + jitter, up to `MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS`), 4xx errors treated as non-retryable, 5xx/network errors retried.\n- 10-second polling cycle that starts only when all detail fetches for the current page have completed.\n- Round-robin concurrency control capped at 5 concurrent detail requests: as one request completes, the next pending job is fetched, keeping at most 5 in flight until all in-progress jobs on the page are updated.\n- Only jobs in a non-terminal state on the currently displayed table page are polled (client-side pagination: default 20 rows, options 5/10/20 per `tablePaginationConstants.ts`); changing the page immediately retargets which jobs are polled.\n- Page Visibility API integration: polling pauses when the browser tab is backgrounded and a single polling cycle triggers immediately when the tab regains focus.\n- Exposure of polling error state (and last successful data) for the warning UI, while the round-robin continues with the next job when a single request fails.\n- Validation that the odh-dashboard BFF proxy transparently passes all detail response fields through unchanged (no BFF code change expected — verification only), including simulating 5xx errors from the BFF to validate the retry pattern in the eval-hub-ui Module Federation context.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Only jobs in a non-terminal state on the currently displayed table page are fetched via the detail endpoint; changing the table page immediately updates which jobs are targeted.\n- At most 5 detail requests are in flight concurrently, dispatched round-robin (the next pending job is fetched as one completes).\n- The 10-second timer for the next cycle starts only after all detail fetches for the current page complete.\n- No network requests to the detail endpoint are made while the browser tab is backgrounded, and a single polling cycle triggers immediately on tab focus, measured via browser dev tools Network tab.\n- On a 5xx or network error, the last successfully fetched data is preserved, the failed request retries with exponential backoff (up to 5 retries), 4xx errors are not retried, and the round-robin continues with the next in-progress job.\n- The odh-dashboard BFF proxy passes all detail response fields through unchanged, verified against the detail endpoint response schema.\n- Retry and backoff behavior is validated in the eval-hub-ui Module Federation context by simulating 5xx errors from the BFF on individual detail endpoints.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Covers the P0 auto-refresh requirement's detail-polling portion (new detail endpoint polling for in-progress job progress).\n- Covers the P0 non-blocking error handling requirement's retry/backoff and last-successful-state preservation portion.\n- Covers the P1 Page Visibility pause/resume requirement.\n- Carries the passive odh-dashboard BFF component's field-passthrough validation.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":56257,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92f56919d3942a78","agent_id":"af27bab92b4583410","session_id":"4d1cfcd2-7a48-4a97-8f21-5ac7a29e76ba","uuid":"e05de49f-adee-4b89-b3ef-b41ae3fc8ded","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:33:50.185Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
