{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-1ece4104-734f-4b0a-86b5-3ec4d7a4e88d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b35d36ae16a978b8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-yo4xeveb/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-BRANCH-A-E006.md","content":"# Benchmark Progress, Elapsed Time, and Polling Warning Display\n\n## Description\n\nRender benchmark-level progress, elapsed time, and the non-blocking warning for temporarily unavailable status updates on the EvalHub Evaluations landing page, using the data exposed by the detail-polling layer. This epic exists only in the decomposition branch where the investigation confirms that `status.benchmarks[]` is populated while a job is still running; it consumes per-benchmark status and timestamp data from the detail endpoint of in-progress jobs on the visible table page.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs, expressed as \"Benchmarks: X/N complete\", where X is the count of entries in `status.benchmarks[]` with `status: \"completed\"` from the detail response.\n- Elapsed time display for running jobs, computed client-side as the difference between the current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` timestamp across all benchmarks (falling back to `resource.created_at` when no benchmark has started), rendered per the approved UX specification.\n- Behavior before the first detail fetch returns for a given job: only the top-level state from the list endpoint is shown (no benchmark progress or elapsed time).\n- Non-blocking inline warning (PatternFly Alert, warning variant) displayed while detail polling encounters errors, indicating that status updates are temporarily unavailable, while the last successfully fetched data continues to be displayed.\n- Rendering per the approved UX specification's progress indicator and warning patterns, including the single-benchmark case where elapsed time is the primary progress indicator.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an evaluation job is in the running state with 3 of 5 benchmarks completed, when a user views the Evaluations landing page and the detail-polling cycle has completed for that job, then benchmark-level progress is displayed (e.g., \"Benchmarks: 3/5 complete\"), measured by the count matching the number of entries in the `status.benchmarks[]` array with `status: \"completed\"` in the detail response.\n- Given an evaluation job has been running for 4 minutes, when the detail-polling cycle has fetched the job's detail endpoint, then elapsed time is displayed (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\"), measured by the elapsed time being the difference between the current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` timestamp in the detail response.\n- Given the EvalHub Server is temporarily unreachable during detail polling, when the frontend encounters a 5xx or network error on a detail fetch, then the last successfully fetched benchmark progress remains displayed and a non-blocking inline warning Alert is visible.\n- Display patterns match the approved UX specification.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Covers the P1 benchmark-level progress display requirement.\n- Covers the P1 elapsed time display requirement (computed from per-benchmark `started_at`).\n- Covers the inline-warning-display portion of the P0 non-blocking error handling requirement.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":57257,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92f56919d3942a78","agent_id":"af27bab92b4583410","session_id":"4d1cfcd2-7a48-4a97-8f21-5ac7a29e76ba","uuid":"1f34c5fa-515f-4f15-9160-815e7cd4a304","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:34:02.597Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
