{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba2524da19887daa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: mid-run population of status.benchmarks[] in the EvalHub Server\n4\t  detail endpoint'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n6\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n7\tteam: TrustyAI / EvalHub\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Investigation: Mid-Run Population of `status.benchmarks[]` in the EvalHub Server Detail Endpoint\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tDetermine whether the EvalHub Server's job detail endpoint (`GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}`) populates the `status.benchmarks[]` array with per-benchmark status entries (`started_at`, `completed_at`, per-benchmark `status`) while an evaluation job is still running, or only after job completion. This is an explicit open question in the strategy, and its answer selects between two decomposition branches for the progress-display work: if populated mid-run, the detail-polling layer and benchmark-level progress display proceed as designed; if populated only at completion, no mid-run detail polling is warranted and elapsed time is computed from `resource.created_at` in the list endpoint response instead.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Inspect the EvalHub Server source code and the published API reference for the detail endpoint to determine when `status.benchmarks[]` entries are written (during job execution vs. at completion), citing specific source locations.\n35\t- Where source inspection is inconclusive, run a job against a development instance of the EvalHub Server and inspect the detail response while the job is in a non-terminal state.\n36\t- Document the determination and the selected outcome: (A) populated mid-run, or (B) populated only at completion.\n37\t- State which downstream progress-display work exists under the resolved outcome so the implementation team can plan accordingly.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- Given the EvalHub Server source code (and, if needed, a running development instance), when an evaluation job is in a running state, then it is documented whether `status.benchmarks[]` contains per-benchmark status entries mid-run, measured by a written determination citing specific source locations or an observed response payload.\n42\t- The branch decision (mid-run populated vs. completion-only) is recorded and communicated, with the impact on the detail-polling and progress-display work stated explicitly.\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- Gates the P0 auto-refresh requirement's detail-polling portion and the P1 benchmark-level progress display requirement: the answer determines whether the detail-polling layer exists and whether benchmark progress is displayable mid-run.\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-abc2331d3c3819ed","agent_id":"a836b225646a1f998","session_id":"4d1cfcd2-7a48-4a97-8f21-5ac7a29e76ba","uuid":"a4db0163-fbda-470c-9fdb-bc8d6f667aa1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:37:37.716Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba2524da19887daa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
