{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a26c7c56cc96f8ef","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E002\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: status.message.message_code values for pre-start vs. runtime\n4\t  failures'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n6\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n7\tteam: TrustyAI / EvalHub\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P2\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Investigation: `status.message.message_code` Values for Pre-Start vs. Runtime Failures\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tEnumerate the values that `status.message.message_code` takes in the EvalHub Server job responses for pre-start failures (admission errors, resource quota exceeded, scheduling failures) versus runtime failures (failures after execution has started), and determine whether the UI can reliably distinguish the two failure classes. This is an explicit open question in the strategy: the answer decides whether the pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction feature is implemented, or whether the documented fallback (a single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail) is used.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Inspect the EvalHub Server source code for where `status.message.message_code` values are produced, and enumerate the codes for admission errors, resource quota failures, scheduling failures, and runtime errors.\n35\t- Where source inspection is inconclusive, trigger representative failure scenarios against a development instance and record the observed `message_code` values.\n36\t- Classify each enumerated code as pre-start failure, runtime failure, or ambiguous/unknown.\n37\t- Document the determination: (A) the code set reliably distinguishes pre-start from runtime failures, or (B) it does not, in which case the fallback rendering applies.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- Given the EvalHub Server source (and, if needed, observed failure responses), then a table of `message_code` values classified as pre-start failure, runtime failure, or ambiguous is produced, measured by each classification citing a source location or observed payload.\n42\t- The determination of whether a reliable pre-start vs. runtime distinction is possible is recorded and communicated, with the impact on the failure-state UI stated explicitly.\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- Gates the P2 requirement for pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction: the answer determines whether that feature is implemented or the single-\"Failed\"-state fallback is used.\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-abc2331d3c3819ed","agent_id":"a836b225646a1f998","session_id":"4d1cfcd2-7a48-4a97-8f21-5ac7a29e76ba","uuid":"8e5f129e-7357-4d85-865e-8edda7086ecd","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:37:38.784Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a26c7c56cc96f8ef","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
