{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a07e8bdd411eed9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-BRANCH-A-E006\n3\ttitle: Benchmark progress, elapsed time, and polling warning display\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-BRANCH-A-E005\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If status.benchmarks[] is not populated mid-run, benchmark X/N\n17\t    progress is not displayable mid-run; elapsed-time-only display from resource.created_at\n18\t    is delivered instead (branch B).\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 4\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Benchmark Progress, Elapsed Time, and Polling Warning Display\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tRender benchmark-level progress, elapsed time, and the non-blocking warning for temporarily unavailable status updates on the EvalHub Evaluations landing page, using the data exposed by the detail-polling layer. This epic exists only in the decomposition branch where the investigation confirms that `status.benchmarks[]` is populated while a job is still running; it consumes per-benchmark status and timestamp data from the detail endpoint of in-progress jobs on the visible table page.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs, expressed as \"Benchmarks: X/N complete\", where X is the count of entries in `status.benchmarks[]` with `status: \"completed\"` from the detail response.\n44\t- Elapsed time display for running jobs, computed client-side as the difference between the current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` timestamp across all benchmarks (falling back to `resource.created_at` when no benchmark has started), rendered per the approved UX specification.\n45\t- Behavior before the first detail fetch returns for a given job: only the top-level state from the list endpoint is shown (no benchmark progress or elapsed time).\n46\t- Non-blocking inline warning (PatternFly Alert, warning variant) displayed while detail polling encounters errors, indicating that status updates are temporarily unavailable, while the last successfully fetched data continues to be displayed.\n47\t- Rendering per the approved UX specification's progress indicator and warning patterns, including the single-benchmark case where elapsed time is the primary progress indicator.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Given an evaluation job is in the running state with 3 of 5 benchmarks completed, when a user views the Evaluations landing page and the detail-polling cycle has completed for that job, then benchmark-level progress is displayed (e.g., \"Benchmarks: 3/5 complete\"), measured by the count matching the number of entries in the `status.benchmarks[]` array with `status: \"completed\"` in the detail response.\n52\t- Given an evaluation job has been running for 4 minutes, when the detail-polling cycle has fetched the job's detail endpoint, then elapsed time is displayed (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\"), measured by the elapsed time being the difference between the current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` timestamp in the detail response.\n53\t- Given the EvalHub Server is temporarily unreachable during detail polling, when the frontend encounters a 5xx or network error on a detail fetch, then the last successfully fetched benchmark progress remains displayed and a non-blocking inline warning Alert is visible.\n54\t- Display patterns match the approved UX specification.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- Covers the P1 benchmark-level progress display requirement.\n59\t- Covers the P1 elapsed time display requirement (computed from per-benchmark `started_at`).\n60\t- Covers the inline-warning-display portion of the P0 non-blocking error handling requirement.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-abc2331d3c3819ed","agent_id":"a836b225646a1f998","session_id":"4d1cfcd2-7a48-4a97-8f21-5ac7a29e76ba","uuid":"61029866-67e0-4d3f-8e90-a34b2fc01b3c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:37:45.853Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a07e8bdd411eed9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
