{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be87f216a663aec6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-BRANCH-B-E005\n3\ttitle: Elapsed time display from job creation timestamp\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If status.benchmarks[] is populated mid-run (branch A), this\n16\t    epic is dropped; elapsed time is computed from per-benchmark started_at in the\n17\t    detail response alongside benchmark-level progress.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Elapsed Time Display from Job Creation Timestamp\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tDisplay elapsed time for running evaluation jobs on the EvalHub Evaluations landing page, computed from `resource.created_at` available in the existing list endpoint response. This epic exists only in the decomposition branch where the investigation determines that `status.benchmarks[]` is populated only after job completion: in that outcome, mid-run detail polling provides no progress value, so no detail-polling layer is built, and elapsed time from the job creation timestamp is the primary progress indicator alongside the top-level state from list polling.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Elapsed time display for jobs in a non-terminal state, computed client-side as the difference between the current time and `resource.created_at` from the list endpoint, rendered per the approved UX specification.\n43\t- Elapsed time acting as the primary progress indicator for running jobs (including single-benchmark jobs), per the strategy's risk mitigation.\n44\t- State display from the existing list endpoint polling (30-second interval) — no mid-run requests to the detail endpoint.\n45\t- Rendering per the approved UX specification's progress indicator pattern.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Given an evaluation job has been running for 4 minutes, when a user views the Evaluations landing page, then elapsed time is displayed, measured by the elapsed time being the difference between the current time and the job's `resource.created_at` from the list endpoint response.\n50\t- No network requests are made to the detail endpoint for mid-run job progress.\n51\t- The display matches the approved UX specification.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- Covers the P1 elapsed time display requirement in its degraded (list-data-only) form.\n56\t- Under this branch, the P0 auto-refresh requirement is met by the existing list endpoint polling for top-level state transitions.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-abc2331d3c3819ed","agent_id":"a836b225646a1f998","session_id":"4d1cfcd2-7a48-4a97-8f21-5ac7a29e76ba","uuid":"fce20d14-8b89-49e7-8d18-0afd961f2dcf","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:37:47.525Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-be87f216a663aec6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
