{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a267623c537521de","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-BRANCH-A-E005\n3\ttitle: Detail-polling data layer for visible-page evaluation jobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If status.benchmarks[] is not populated mid-run, no mid-run detail\n16\t    polling is built; elapsed time is computed from resource.created_at in the list\n17\t    endpoint response instead (branch B).\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Detail-Polling Data Layer for Visible-Page Evaluation Jobs\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tImplement the second polling layer in the eval-hub-ui plugin: a detail-polling hook that fetches the detail endpoint (`GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}`) for in-progress jobs visible on the currently displayed table page, obtaining `status.benchmarks[]` per-benchmark progress data for display. This epic exists only in the decomposition branch where the investigation confirms that `status.benchmarks[]` is populated while a job is still running; under the alternative outcome, mid-run detail polling has no value and is not built.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- New detail-polling hook in the eval-hub-ui plugin following the React Query retry-with-backoff pattern established by the autorag package (`usePipelineRunQuery`): `placeholderData` preserving the last successful response during transient errors, retry with exponential backoff (`RETRY_DELAY_MS * 2^attempt` + jitter, up to `MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS`), 4xx errors treated as non-retryable, 5xx/network errors retried.\n43\t- 10-second polling cycle that starts only when all detail fetches for the current page have completed.\n44\t- Round-robin concurrency control capped at 5 concurrent detail requests: as one request completes, the next pending job is fetched, keeping at most 5 in flight until all in-progress jobs on the page are updated.\n45\t- Only jobs in a non-terminal state on the currently displayed table page are polled (client-side pagination: default 20 rows, options 5/10/20 per `tablePaginationConstants.ts`); changing the page immediately retargets which jobs are polled.\n46\t- Page Visibility API integration: polling pauses when the browser tab is backgrounded and a single polling cycle triggers immediately when the tab regains focus.\n47\t- Exposure of polling error state (and last successful data) for the warning UI, while the round-robin continues with the next job when a single request fails.\n48\t- Validation that the odh-dashboard BFF proxy transparently passes all detail response fields through unchanged (no BFF code change expected — verification only), including simulating 5xx errors from the BFF to validate the retry pattern in the eval-hub-ui Module Federation context.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Only jobs in a non-terminal state on the currently displayed table page are fetched via the detail endpoint; changing the table page immediately updates which jobs are targeted.\n53\t- At most 5 detail requests are in flight concurrently, dispatched round-robin (the next pending job is fetched as one completes).\n54\t- The 10-second timer for the next cycle starts only after all detail fetches for the current page complete.\n55\t- No network requests to the detail endpoint are made while the browser tab is backgrounded, and a single polling cycle triggers immediately on tab focus, measured via browser dev tools Network tab.\n56\t- On a 5xx or network error, the last successfully fetched data is preserved, the failed request retries with exponential backoff (up to 5 retries), 4xx errors are not retried, and the round-robin continues with the next in-progress job.\n57\t- The odh-dashboard BFF proxy passes all detail response fields through unchanged, verified against the detail endpoint response schema.\n58\t- Retry and backoff behavior is validated in the eval-hub-ui Module Federation context by simulating 5xx errors from the BFF on individual detail endpoints.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- Covers the P0 auto-refresh requirement's detail-polling portion (new detail endpoint polling for in-progress job progress).\n63\t- Covers the P0 non-blocking error handling requirement's retry/backoff and last-successful-state preservation portion.\n64\t- Covers the P1 Page Visibility pause/resume requirement.\n65\t- Carries the passive odh-dashboard BFF component's field-passthrough validation.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83c3fc0004f5a67f","agent_id":"a0ccc90171ba1f7fa","session_id":"4d1cfcd2-7a48-4a97-8f21-5ac7a29e76ba","uuid":"436c6467-c6ef-4051-8c49-b62951fd3fa2","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:45:19.875Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a267623c537521de","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
