ated code table.\n44\t- Distinct icon, color, and label for the pre-start failure treatment per the approved UX specification, visually distinct from the runtime \"Failed\" state.\n45\t- Supplementary display of `status.message` text for failed jobs.\n46\t- Fallback to the single \"Failed\" rendering (with `status.message` text) for codes classified as ambiguous or absent.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Given an evaluation job failed before execution started (e.g., an admission error indicated by `status.message.message_code`), when a user views the Evaluations landing page, then the job row displays a distinct visual treatment differentiating it from a job that ran and then failed, measured by a label reflecting the failure type and an icon/color distinct from the runtime \"Failed\" state.\n51\t- The classification covers the `message_code` values enumerated by the investigation; ambiguous or absent codes fall back to the single \"Failed\" rendering with `status.message` text as supplementary detail.\n52\t- Visual treatments match the approved UX specification.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- Covers the P2 requirement for pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction using `status.message.message_code`.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83c3fc0004f5a67f","agent_id":"a0ccc90171ba1f7fa","session_id":"4d1cfcd2-7a48-4a97-8f21-5ac7a29e76ba","uuid":"269ed630-4920-4baf-be92-0d1b3dffc264","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:45:20.824Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-90b17e53f9ad06bf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
