{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2a19415de396bb8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E005\n3\ttitle: Detail-polling data layer for visible-page evaluation jobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: null\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If status.benchmarks[] is not populated mid-run, no mid-run detail\n16\t    polling is built; elapsed time is computed from resource.created_at in the list\n17\t    endpoint response instead (see the elapsed-time-from-created-at epic).\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Detail-Polling Data Layer for Visible-Page Evaluation Jobs\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tImplement the second polling layer in the eval-hub-ui plugin: a detail-polling hook that fetches the detail endpoint (`GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}`) for in-progress jobs visible on the currently displayed table page, obtaining `status.benchmarks[]` per-benchmark progress data for display. This epic exists only in the decomposition branch where the investigation confirms that `status.benchmarks[]` is populated while a job is still running; under the alternative outcome, mid-run detail polling has no value and is not built.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- New detail-polling hook in the eval-hub-ui plugin following the React Query retry-with-backoff pattern established by the autorag package (`usePipelineRunQuery`): `placeholderData` preserving the last successful response during transient errors, retry with exponential backoff (`RETRY_DELAY_MS * 2^attempt` + jitter, up to `MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS`), 4xx errors treated as non-retryable, 5xx/network errors retried.\n43\t- 10-second polling cycle that starts only when all detail fetches for the current page have completed.\n44\t- Round-robin concurrency control capped at 5 concurrent detail requests: as one request completes, the next pending job is fetched, keeping at most 5 in flight until all in-progress jobs on the page are updated.\n45\t- Only jobs in a non-terminal state on the currently displayed table page are polled (client-side pagination: default 20 rows, options 5/10/20 per `tablePaginationConstants.ts`); changing the page immediately retargets which jobs are polled."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83c3fc0004f5a67f","agent_id":"a0ccc90171ba1f7fa","session_id":"4d1cfcd2-7a48-4a97-8f21-5ac7a29e76ba","uuid":"9e08084a-e98f-4e88-b04f-fc86ee6cfafd","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:49:18.537Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2a19415de396bb8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
