{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8222a0db4e0b5152","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E006\n3\ttitle: Benchmark progress, elapsed time, and polling warning display\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: null\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E003\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E005\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: remove\n17\t  fallback_approach: If status.benchmarks[] is not populated mid-run, benchmark X/N\n18\t    progress is not displayable mid-run; elapsed-time-only display from resource.created_at\n19\t    is delivered instead (see the elapsed-time-from-created-at epic).\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: 1\n26\t  external_dependency: 0\n27\t  human_process_gates: -1\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 5\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Benchmark Progress, Elapsed Time, and Polling Warning Display\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tRender benchmark-level progress, elapsed time, and the non-blocking warning for temporarily unavailable status updates on the EvalHub Evaluations landing page, using the data exposed by the detail-polling layer. This epic is gated by the mid-run data-availability investigation and exists only in the outcome where the investigation confirms that `status.benchmarks[]` is populated while a job is still running; it consumes per-benchmark status and timestamp data from the detail endpoint of in-progress jobs on the visible table page, and renders per the UX specification.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs, expressed as \"Benchmarks: X/N complete\", where X is the count of entries in `status.benchmarks[]` with `status: \"completed\"` from the detail response.\n45\t- Elapsed time display for running jobs, computed client-side as the difference between the current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` timestamp across all benchmarks (falling back to `resource.created_at` when no benchmark has started), rendered per the approved UX specification.\n46\t- Behavior before the first detail fetch returns for a given job: only the top-level state from the list endpoint is shown (no benchmark progress or elapsed time).\n47\t- Non-blocking inline warning (PatternFly Alert, warning variant) displayed while detail polling encounters errors, indicating that status updates are temporarily unavailable, while the last successfully fetched data continues to be displayed.\n48\t- Rendering per the approved UX specification's progress indicator and warning patterns, including the single-benchmark case where elapsed time is the primary progress indicator.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Given an evaluation job is in the running state with 3 of 5 benchmarks completed, when a user views the Evaluations landing page and the detail-polling cycle has completed for that job, then benchmark-level progress is displayed (e.g., \"Benchmarks: 3/5 complete\"), measured by the count matching the number of entries in the `status.benchmarks[]` array with `status: \"completed\"` in the detail response.\n53\t- Given an evaluation job has been running for 4 minutes, when the detail-polling cycle has fetched the job's detail endpoint, then elapsed time is displayed (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\"), measured by the elapsed time being the difference between the current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` timestamp in the detail response.\n54\t- Given the EvalHub Server is temporarily unreachable during detail polling, when the frontend encounters a 5xx or network error on a detail fetch, then the last successfully fetched benchmark progress remains displayed and a non-blocking inline warning Alert is visible.\n55\t- Display patterns match the approved UX specification.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- Covers the P1 benchmark-level progress display requirement.\n60\t- Covers the P1 elapsed time display requirement (computed from per-benchmark `started_at`).\n61\t- Covers the inline-warning-display portion of the P0 non-blocking error handling requirement.\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99aea0eeced0803c","agent_id":"a658e2710e15ff1a2","session_id":"4d1cfcd2-7a48-4a97-8f21-5ac7a29e76ba","uuid":"c9a40dc6-0459-432c-87b3-4fe556a17afa","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:52:47.464Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8222a0db4e0b5152","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
