{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99aa2f983c7c4733","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E007\n3\ttitle: Pre-start vs. runtime failure state distinction\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tbranch: null\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E002\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E002\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E003\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If message_code does not reliably distinguish failure types,\n17\t    the distinction is dropped; the single 'Failed' state with status.message text\n18\t    as supplementary detail (fallback acceptance criterion on the state differentiation\n19\t    epic) is used.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: 1\n26\t  external_dependency: 0\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 6\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Pre-Start vs. Runtime Failure State Distinction\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tDistinguish evaluation jobs that failed before execution started (admission errors, resource quota exceeded, scheduling failures) from jobs that ran and then failed, in the job table's state rendering, using the `status.message.message_code` values enumerated by the failure-code investigation. This epic is gated by the failure-code investigation and exists only in the outcome where that investigation confirms the code set reliably distinguishes pre-start from runtime failures.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Label and rendering logic that classifies failed jobs as \"Failed (not started)\" versus \"Failed\" (runtime) based on the `status.message.message_code` classification from the investigation's enumerated code table.\n45\t- Distinct icon, color, and label for the pre-start failure treatment per the approved UX specification, visually distinct from the runtime \"Failed\" state.\n46\t- Supplementary display of `status.message` text for failed jobs.\n47\t- Fallback to the single \"Failed\" rendering (with `status.message` text) for codes classified as ambiguous or absent.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Given an evaluation job failed before execution started (e.g., an admission error indicated by `status.message.message_code`), when a user views the Evaluations landing page, then the job row displays a distinct visual treatment differentiating it from a job that ran and then failed, measured by a label reflecting the failure type and an icon/color distinct from the runtime \"Failed\" state.\n52\t- The classification covers the `message_code` values enumerated by the investigation; ambiguous or absent codes fall back to the single \"Failed\" rendering with `status.message` text as supplementary detail.\n53\t- Visual treatments match the approved UX specification.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- Covers the P2 requirement for pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction using `status.message.message_code`.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99aea0eeced0803c","agent_id":"a658e2710e15ff1a2","session_id":"4d1cfcd2-7a48-4a97-8f21-5ac7a29e76ba","uuid":"98fc4ee8-3fd0-4f14-a3b5-ac801b283d1f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:52:48.386Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-99aa2f983c7c4733","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
