on-terminal state, computed client-side as the difference between the current time and `resource.created_at` from the list endpoint, rendered per the approved UX specification.\n44\t- Elapsed time acting as the primary progress indicator for running jobs (including single-benchmark jobs), per the strategy's risk mitigation.\n45\t- State display from the existing list endpoint polling (30-second interval) — no mid-run requests to the detail endpoint.\n46\t- Rendering per the approved UX specification's progress indicator pattern.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Given an evaluation job has been running for 4 minutes, when a user views the Evaluations landing page, then elapsed time is displayed, measured by the elapsed time being the difference between the current time and the job's `resource.created_at` from the list endpoint response.\n51\t- No network requests are made to the detail endpoint for mid-run job progress.\n52\t- The display matches the approved UX specification.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- Covers the P1 elapsed time display requirement in its degraded (list-data-only) form.\n57\t- Under this branch, the P0 auto-refresh requirement is met by the existing list endpoint polling for top-level state transitions.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99aea0eeced0803c","agent_id":"a658e2710e15ff1a2","session_id":"4d1cfcd2-7a48-4a97-8f21-5ac7a29e76ba","uuid":"dab0362d-c9f3-41f7-93d4-293fe3a75829","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:52:49.104Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-949a71e4dc81c6be","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
